   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of Olean to\nimpose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal of such provisions\nupon the expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6671",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6671-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-uu, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6671A\n\nSPONSOR: BORRELLO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of\nOlean to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal of\nsuch provisions upon the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would require meetings held between the Speaker of the Assem-\nbly, Temporary President of the Senate, and the Governor to discuss,\nnegotiate, or debate, in part or in its entirety, the provisions of the\nstate budget to be open to the public.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Creates a new section 103-B of the Public Officers Law to\nrequire meetings between the legislative leaders and the governor to be\nopen to the public, the host of the meeting to provide the public to\nattend the meeting in at least one physical location at which a member\nparticipates, and requires meetings to be broadcast to the public when\npracticable.\n\nSection 2: establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nToo often, the state budget process is shrouded in speculation, rumor,\nand closed-door negotiation only to be revealed in drips and drabs in\ncomments to the press with no concern for public input or timeliness.\nThis legislation would add sunlight and accountability to the budget\nnegotiation process by requiring the leaders of each house of the legis-\nlature and the governor to openly discuss the budget in front of the\npeople they each represent.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
